    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d327">

                <pb facs="0270" n="198" sameAs="frus:frus1865p4/pg198"/>

                <head>Municipal Council of Dorchester</head>
                <p rendition="#flush">Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams</hi>, <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">United States Minister at the Court of St. James:</hi>
                </p>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: We, the mayor, aldermen, and burgesses of
                    the borough of Dorchester, in the county of Dorset, in council assembled, beg to
                    approach your excellency with an expression of our deepest indignation and
                    horror at the recent murder of the President of the United States of America,
                    and the attempted assassination of Mr. Secretary Seward under circumstances of
                    unheard of atrocity, and we desire through you to offer to Mrs. Lincoln our
                    respectful and heartfelt condolence under her sad and awful bereavement; to Mr.
                    Seward our sincere congratulations <pb facs="0271" n="199" xml:id="pg199"/> at
                    his providential escape; and to him and the American people our genuine sympathy
                    with them at the loss of a ruler of whom Americans were so justly proud.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">Given under the common seal of the borough of
                            <placeName>Dorchester</placeName> the <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1865-05-02">2d day of May, 1865</date>.</dateline>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#small-caps">seal</hi>.] <signed>JOHN PETTY ALDRIDGEHED, </signed>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mayor</hi>. </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
